-- title:
--   Factoring out a constant from the kernel of a reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a valuation ring, let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism to a field $k$, let $E$ be a commutative ring, $\varphi : A \to E$ a ring homomorphism and $X, Y \in E$. Let $P \in (A[x])[y]$ be monic in $y$ with $0 < \deg_y P$, and suppose $P$ vanishes when $y$ is evaluated at $Y$ and the coefficients in $A[x]$ are sent to $E$ by $\varphi$ together with $x \mapsto X$. Let $R$ be a subring of $E$ containing $X$, $Y$ and all $\varphi(a)$ for $a \in A$, and contained in the subring of $E$ generated by the image of $\varphi$ together with $X$ and $Y$. Let $S$ be a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure and $\mathrm{red}_0 : R \to S$ a ring homomorphism with $\mathrm{red}_0(\varphi(a)) = \mathrm{red}(a)$ in $S$ for all $a \in A$, such that $\mathrm{red}_0(X)$ is transcendental over $k$ and the relative degree of $k(\mathrm{red}_0 X, \mathrm{red}_0 Y)$ over $k(\mathrm{red}_0 X)$, both taken as intermediate fields of $S/k$, equals $\deg_y P$. Then for every $r \in R$ with $\mathrm{red}_0(r) = 0$ there are $m \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}(m) = 0$ and $r' \in R$ such that $r = \varphi(m) \, r'$.
--
--   This is the algebraic core of the comparison between a model of a modular curve over a valuation ring and its reduction: under the stated degree and transcendence conditions the reduction map on the two-generator ring $R$ has kernel generated by the constants killed by $\mathrm{red}$, so any element reducing to zero acquires a factor coming from $A$. It is applied, in the form of the localised reduction homomorphism and its inverse variant, by [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero) and [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_inv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.exists_eq_const_mul_of_modularRedLocHom_eq_zero_inv).
